{"id": "6d48295f-1e80-4eb7-b858-dfe3bfb36ffd", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit SageMaker notebook instances and Studio domains for internet exposure and encryption at rest. The audit covers the associated accounts and the regions where SageMaker resources exist. It's read-only, so nothing will change. I'll report back with the findings.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_f5mJUo38hcL7PvntKqV1Xw", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-exposure-encryption-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only audit of Amazon SageMaker notebook instances and SageMaker domains (Studio) for (1) internet exposure and (2) encryption at rest. Return a concise, severity-rated findings table plus a short remediation summary.",
  "context": "User asked: 'Audit our SageMaker notebooks and domains for internet exposure and encryption at rest'. Use list_associations to find every AWS account associated with this agent space (the agent space's home account is 012345678901_1, region us-east-1; workloads can be in other associated accounts). For each account, check the regions where SageMaker resources exist (start with us-east-1 and any other regions in common use; probe additional enabled regions efficiently, e.g. via list_notebook_instances/list_domains in each region). Use only non-mutating operations. Do not attempt any changes.",
  "resources": ["SageMaker notebook instances", "SageMaker domains, user profiles, and spaces", "Associated security groups, subnets, VPCs, and KMS keys"],
  "timeframe": "Current state as of 2026-11-15",
  "criteria": "Notebook instances (list_notebook_instances, describe_notebook_instance): flag DirectInternetAccess=Enabled; no SubnetId/VPC attachment; RootAccess enabled; KmsKeyId missing (volume encryption uses no CMK); security groups with 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 ingress; public-IP subnets (MapPublicIpOnLaunch / route to IGW); IMDSv1 allowed (InstanceMetadataServiceConfiguration MinimumInstanceMetadataServiceVersion != 2). Domains (list_domains, describe_domain; also list_user_profiles/list_spaces where relevant): flag AppNetworkAccessType=PublicInternetOnly (vs VpcOnly); missing KmsKeyId on the domain (EFS home directory encrypted with AWS-managed key rather than CMK); SecurityGroupIds with open ingress 0.0.0.0/0; subnets with IGW routes and no VPC endpoints (sagemaker.api, sagemaker.runtime, studio/notebook) where VpcOnly; DefaultUserSettings/ DefaultSpaceSettings missing encryption or with open egress; domains with no VPC. Also, where easily checked, note related endpoints/training jobs are out of scope. For each finding give: account, region, resource name, issue, severity (High/Medium/Low), and a one-line remediation. Also report totals of resources scanned per account/region and note any account/region you could not access (permission errors) so coverage gaps are explicit. Note: encryption at rest on SageMaker notebooks is always on for the volume with an AWS-managed key by default only if KmsKeyId is set - verify by documentation via verify_aws_claim if unsure, and state clearly the difference between 'AWS-managed default' and 'customer-managed KMS key'. Keep the report concise; do not dump raw API output."
}", "preloaded_skills": ["discovering-topology", "verifying-with-docs"]}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit SageMaker notebooks and domains for exposure and encryption"}], "created_at": null}

